## Category F: Performance & Usability

**17. The 6-section pill bar is too wide on standard screens.**
Six sections ("Action Center", "Pulse", "Incidents & triage", "Timeline & movers", "Freshness & replay", "Entity 360") create a crowded pill bar that wraps on screens < 1400px. Shorten labels: "Actions", "Pulse", "Incidents", "Timeline", "Freshness", "Entity".

*Reasoning:* "Incidents & triage" is 17 characters; "Incidents" is 9. On the primary triage page that a DBA visits 5x/day, every pixel of navigation width matters. The meaning is clear from the shorter form.

**18. The batch-fetch pattern (run_batch) should also cover the Timeline section.**
Lines 141-156 (Day Replay) use run_batch for parallel reads. But the Timeline section (event_timeline + spend movers) makes sequential reads. Apply the same parallel batch pattern.

*Reasoning:* The Timeline & Movers section is the second most common investigation path (after Pulse). Serial reads here add 2-4 seconds of sequential latency that parallel batching would eliminate.

**19. The "section_filter_contract" explanations are too verbose for repeated visitors.**
Lines 319-350: every section shows which filters apply/don't apply. This is useful on first visit but becomes noise on the 50th visit. Collapse these into a small icon tooltip (ⓘ) instead of inline captions that take vertical space on every load.

*Reasoning:* Filter applicability is important to understand once. After that, it's chrome noise that pushes actual data below the fold. Progressive disclosure: show it on hover/click, not always.

**20. Add "time in this state" to the Freshness board.**
Line 229-271: Freshness shows STATUS (OK/STALE/NOT LOADED) and HOURS_SINCE_LOAD. But it doesn't show "how long has this source BEEN stale?" A source that went stale 10 minutes ago is different from one that's been stale for 3 days. Add a "STALE_SINCE" column.

*Reasoning:* HOURS_SINCE_LOAD tells you when data last arrived. STALE_SINCE tells you when the problem started. The former is a measurement; the latter is the incident duration. A DBA triaging stale sources needs to know which ones just broke (investigate now) vs which ones have been broken for days (probably known, lower priority).

